{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cd2d7knoUBeij5qUzcTAf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**VERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED, findings=7** — written to `docs/reviews/042-CRITIQUE.md` and committed (`56796ea`, all pre-commit checks passed).\n\nI regenerated `PROJECT_STATE.html` myself and judged the emitted markup, event wiring, and computed contrast ratios (a static-markup inspection, not a visual render — disclosed in the verdict file; no finding rests on pixel-level judgment).\n\nThe two blockers:\n\n1. **Dead When-tab detail panel (U4/T3/A1).** The `#dag-detail` aside says \"Click a work item to read its detail,\" but the script wires `#dag .wi` nodes — and the emitted When view contains zero of them (it renders drill `.block` nodes with no click handler). The panel never populates, and keyboard users have no path to WI detail at all, while the identical structure works fine in the What and Knowledge tabs.\n2. **Contrast below the declared 4.5:1 floor (A4).** Measured white-on-fill label text: done-green 3.77 (132 blocks), SR-cyan 3.68, amber 3.19, SN-indigo 4.47 — and the 8.5px sub-labels at opacity .85 drop to 2.72–3.95 on five of six fills.\n\nThe majors: WI status encoded by fill hue alone (A3 — \"(done)\" lives only in the hover tooltip); the Knowledge tab opens as a flat wall of all 249 concept nodes with no start-collapsed grouping (T2); the How-SW view ships with neither a legend nor a detail panel while its sibling When view has both (U3); and one hue carrying multiple meanings — `#059669` is simultaneously \"done,\" phase \"v3,\" and \"Test Case\" — which I proposed as new anchor **U5 — one color, one meaning** per the accumulation rule. One minor: per-emitter node-label sizes (9/10/11px) instead of one shared scale (U1).\n\nWhat genuinely passed: T1 (all three reading tasks are one tab switch), keyboard reachability of everything that's actually wired (native tab buttons, `tabindex` + Enter/Space on all descendable blocks, focus-mirrors-hover on all 443 detail-wired nodes), `<title>` accessible names throughout, and start-collapsed drill views in When/How.\n\nI also filed three TC-HARDEN proposals for change-intake: mechanize the contrast check, assert emitted `querySelectorAll` selectors match ≥1 element (would have caught the dead wiring), and require a legend wherever an emitter uses multiple categorical fills."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1417,"cache_read_input_tokens":72015,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1417},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be9205e6-b152-4c68-9389-d7ea12d18f4a","uuid":"35109965-784a-4e50-8a13-5d3b91d4205a","request_id":"req_011Cd2d7gseuGVRX3xgy4xst"}
